course: dictionary
lesson: 2766
title: Discount: a word with three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A discount is money taken off the usual price, so you pay less. «Up to 70% off» tells you the biggest discount is 70%, but only on some things. Most things are cut by less, so read the small print before you get too excited.
explain: To discount is a verb that means to make a price lower. A shop might discount a coat in the January sale. Look at the words around it: if the sentence is about money and shopping, discount means cut the price.
explain: To discount an idea means to think it is not important or not true. If someone says they will discount what you said, they are not talking about money. Context helps you again: the sentence is about thinking, not paying.
fact: A discount is money taken off the usual price, so you pay less.
fact: The sale price is the price minus the discount.
fact: A «half price» sale is a 50% discount, because half of the price is taken off.
fact: Some shops raise a price before a sale so that the discount looks bigger; price-tracking websites show what something really cost before.
fact: «Up to 70% off» means only some things get the biggest discount; most things are cut by less.
exercise: A sign says «half price». What is the discount? | *50% | 2% | 5% | 25%
exercise: Tia says her teacher will discount her idea. What does discount mean here? | Buy it cheaply | Hide it in a box | Make the price lower | *Think it is not important or not true
exercise: A coat costs £40 and the discount is £10. How much do you pay? | £50 | £40 | £10 | *£30
test: A shop raises its price just before a sale. Why might it do this? | Because it is January | So there is no sale at all | So the coat gets cheaper for everyone | *So the discount looks bigger
test: Which word is a noun meaning money taken off a price? | deliver | *discount | design | decide
exam: Ravi sees «Up to 70% off» and thinks every coat is 70% off. Is he right? | *No, the biggest discount is only on some things | Yes, because the sale is on | No, nothing is ever cheaper | Yes, every single thing is 70% off
